   562| * Submit an owner-approved development task to the worker queue with per-owner
   563| * single-flight enforcement. If an active job already exists for the same
   564| * owner, the request ATTACHES to that job (returns its jobId) instead of
   565| * creating a duplicate or returning HTTP 409.
   566| *
   567| * The user's request is NEVER discarded:
   568| *   - If no active job exists → a new job is created and queued.
   569| *   - If an active job exists for the same owner → the request attaches to it.
   570| *   - If the active job is stale → it is expired and a new job is created.
   571| *
   572| * Owner approval MUST already be verified by the caller (API boundary).
   573| */
